         fhir:comment [ fhir:v "Element matches Basic element path `Basic.meta` (`Resource.meta`), use that element instead.\nElement `ActorDefinition.meta` is not mapped to FHIR R4, since FHIR R5 `ActorDefinition` is not mapped.\nElement `ActorDefinition.meta` has no mapping targets in FHIR R4. Typically, this is because the element has been added (is a new element)." ]
       ] )
     ] [
       fhir:code [ fhir:v "ActorDefinition.implicitRules" ] ;
       fhir:display [ fhir:v "implicitRules" ] ;
       fhir:target ( [
         fhir:code [ fhir:v "Basic.implicitRules" ] ;
         fhir:display [ fhir:v "Basic.implicitRules" ] ;
         fhir:equivalence [ fhir:v "equivalent" ] ;
         fhir:comment [ fhir:v "Element matches Basic element path `Basic.implicitRules` (`Resource.implicitRules`), use that element instead.\nElement `ActorDefinition.implicitRules` is not mapped to FHIR R4, since FHIR R5 `ActorDefinition` is not mapped.\nElement `ActorDefinition.implicitRules` has no mapping targets in FHIR R4. Typically, this is because the element has been added (is a new element).\nAsserting this rule set restricts the content to be only understood by a limited set of trading partners. This inherently limits the usefulness of the data in the long term. However, the existing health eco-system is highly fractured, and not yet ready to define, collect, and exchange data in a generally computable sense. Wherever possible, implementers and/or specification writers should avoid using this element. Often, when used, the URL is a reference to an implementation guide that defines these special rules as part of its narrative along with other profiles, value sets, etc." ]
